From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:07:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] mmvq: GDN gate/beta epilogue for non-Q8_0
 ssm_alpha/ssm_beta (GGML_CUDA_FUSE_GDN_EPI=0: off)

Qwen3.5/3.6/3.8 GDN layers whose ssm_alpha/ssm_beta are Q4_K/Q5_K/Q6_K/IQ4_XS/MXFP4 ran the
two small projections, then ADD(dt) -> SOFTPLUS -> MUL(ssm_a) and SIGMOID as separate launches.
The ksplit body now applies that chain in its epilogue (template flag gdn_epi, per row-concat
segment): decode folds it into the existing alpha/beta/z row concat (3 -> 1 launches per GDN
layer), the verify band (2..8 tokens) runs alpha + beta as one row-concat launch with the
epilogue (5 -> 2). Every row keeps its own ksplit dot product (same nwarps / long_k / small_m
as its unfused launch, <= 256 rows so one row per block); the epilogue is the softplus /
sigmoid of unary.cu with rounded add / mul. The graph reorder puts z in front of the small pair.

KLD on vs off (1 GPU, ROCBLAS_USE_HIPBLASLT=0, -ub 1/4/8): mean 0.000000, same top 100 %, max
equal to the off-vs-off process noise; greedy and 30k-depth hashes identical. Decode: 27B
Q4_K_M MTP +0.9 %, plain +0.3 %, 27B MXFP4 MTP +1.0 %, 35B-A3B Q4_K_M +0.4 %.
